# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sched-1 window (the scheduler-side levers; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sched-1 (with the branch tp4/agent-turns merged: see ORDER.txt) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sched-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-sched-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a smoke job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the
# same in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix-gate jobs (T0-T3, S1) do not forward the checkpoint (c2_serving_job.MODEL_ACTIONS): they run the base
# weights, which the tier's mechanics (what is spilled, restored and counted) do not depend on.
# S1 (EXACTNESS of the complete spills, STOP): the concurrent tier plan (c2_prefix_gate.py --plan tier-concurrent: seven seats decoding, a 254k session built and evicted by
# ten 120k floods, then returning beside the seats; the restore audited block by block) on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-sch-all-audit. The flood is what
# the cap of 512 blocks a flush cut in the TC1 card run (3,393 of 3,905 displaced blocks dropped when the 254k restore took its blocks). READ: the plan verdict PASS; the
# line "host tier spill complete on cap_blocks=512 hard_max_blocks=4096" in the container log; the restore's flush as one spill line with blocks above 512 and lifted= above
# 0 (and the counters tier_spill_cap_lifted above 0, tier_spill_dropped_cap 0); every pair IDENTICAL; zero tier_digest_failures and tier_audit_mismatches; no "host tier
# spill failed" line; the largest flush's milliseconds RECORDED (ms a block from sched_report.py: ESTIMATE 0.4 ms once the slab is resident, 1.7 ms while it fills). The
# prefix step does not forward the checkpoint keys: this job runs the base weights. Duration (estimate): 100 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset prefix
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sched-1
C2_PREFIX_PLAN=tier-concurrent
C2_PREFIX_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-sch-all-audit
C2_PREFIX_BASELINE=none
C2_BOX_MINUTES=150
